cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this plugin in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Road Furniture Designer"
abstract: >-
  A QGIS plugin for designing road furniture along a Civil 3D LandXML
  alignment to the Kenya Road Design Manual (2025). It places traffic signs
  by hand or proposes them from the alignment's curves, grades and sight
  distances (RDM 6.2); proposes centre lines, edge lines and road studs on the
  same no-overtaking basis (RDM 6.1), embankment barriers from the corridor
  sections (RDM 1.3 Chapter 12), and details traffic calming features,
  crossings and speed limit zones chosen by the designer (RDM 6.4, RDM 6.2).
  Chainage, offset, side and facing are derived from the alignment and kept
  up to date. It writes a live inventory for quantity take-off, an A3 report
  with plan, long-section and strip sheets, schedules and checks of the
  furniture against the geometry, and a georeferenced DXF that pastes into
  Civil 3D at the true coordinates. Design criteria are open data files.
